userStories.description:
**Goal** — Extend the pipeline event union, reporter contract, CallContext, and configuration with the typed phase-telemetry foundation.

**Motivation** — `IReporter` exposes exactly three hooks — `onRunStart`, `onStoryComplete`, `onRunEnd`; everything inside a story is invisible to reporters.

**Approach** — Telemetry is emitted from the **pipeline event bus**, not from the runtime dispatch-event channel (`src/runtime/dispatch-events.ts`), because reporters are wired to the pipeline bus by existing convention (`wireReporters`).

**Scope** — In: additive event and extension types plus validated reporter defaults. Out: event emitters, reporter fan-out, and exporter behavior belong to US-002 through US-008.

**Interface** — verbatim from the design:
```ts
export interface StoryPhaseCompletedEvent {
  type: "story:phase:completed";
  storyId: string;
  phase: string;                 // op name — same vocabulary as story:step
  outcome: "passed" | "failed" | "skipped" | "error";
  durationMs: number;
  costUsd: number;
  tier?: string;
  testStrategy?: TestStrategy;
  sessionModel?: "single-session" | "three-session";
  details?: PhaseDetails;
}
```
```ts
readonly phaseTelemetry?: {
  readonly testStrategy: TestStrategy;
  readonly sessionModel: "single-session" | "three-session";
  readonly tier: string;
};
```
```ts
interface PhaseEventBase { runId: string; scope: "story" | "run"; phase: string; storyId?: string; }
interface PhaseStartEvent extends PhaseEventBase { startTime: string }
interface PhaseCompleteEvent extends PhaseEventBase { outcome: "passed" | "failed" | "skipped" | "error"; durationMs: number; costUsd: number; tier?: string; testStrategy?: TestStrategy; sessionModel?: "single-session" | "three-session"; details?: PhaseDetails | RunPhaseDetails; }
```
Both hooks optional; existing reporters are unaffected.

**Goal** — Propagate routed metadata to every phase and construct typed authoring, verdict, gate, review, and fix detail payloads.

**Motivation** — `sessionModel`, `testStrategy`, and `tier` are not reachable from `runPhase` as it stands.

**Approach** — Resolution — one readonly input-side slice on `CallContext`, populated where `ctx.routing` is in scope (`execution.ts:89-99`). Every `runPhase` call site inherits it through `ctx`, so correctness does not depend on remembering an argument. `sessionModel` comes from `isThreeSessionStrategy(ctx.routing.testStrategy)` — the existing SSOT. `rectification.ts:236` dispatches via `wrappedCallOp(cycleCtx: FixCycleContext, …)`; the slice must survive that hop.

**Scope** — In: post-clamp tier, routed strategy/session metadata, and all PhaseDetails arms. Out: base event/outcome emission is US-002; reporter mapping/export is US-005 onward.

**Interface** — verbatim:
```ts
type PhaseDetails =
  | { kind: "authoring"; role: "test-writer" | "implementer"; filesChanged: number; isolationPassed?: boolean }
  | { kind: "verdict"; role: "verifier" | "verify-scoped"; passed: boolean; failureCount: number }
  | { kind: "gate"; gate: "greenfield" | "full-suite" | "test-presence" | "lint" | "typecheck"; failureCount: number }
  | { kind: "review"; reviewer: "semantic" | "adversarial"; iteration: number; bySeverity: Record<FindingSeverity, number>; blockingCount: number; advisoryCount: number; items?: ReviewFindingSummary[] }
  | { kind: "fix"; strategy: string; findingsBefore: number; findingsAfter: number };
```
`isolationPassed` is set only when `sessionModel === "three-session"`. Severity keys are `critical`, `error`, `warning`, `info`, `low`, and `unverifiable`; use `isBlockingSeverity(finding.severity, threshold)` for blocking/advisory counts. `items` is populated exclusively when `detail` is `verbose`.
